{
  "answer": "The condition `salary <> 100` excludes NULL because SQL comparisons with NULL evaluate to UNKNOWN, and the WHERE clause filters out rows with UNKNOWN predicates.",
  "insufficient": false,
  "citations": [
    {
      "sectionId": "null-comparison",
      "quote": "Ordinary SQL comparisons involving NULL, including NULL = NULL and NULL <> 5, evaluate to UNKNOWN rather than TRUE or FALSE."
    },
    {
      "sectionId": "null-where",
      "quote": "SQL uses TRUE, FALSE, and UNKNOWN in its three-valued logic. A WHERE clause keeps a row only when its predicate is TRUE; FALSE and UNKNOWN are both filtered out."
    }
  ]
}
